# The mismatch    [section sec1]
CTM's thought representation is compact; super-resolution needs a dense spatial field.

## Method    [section sec2]
A persistent dense carrier, read and updated by a compact thought process.

## Results    [section sec3]
Competitive with CNN baselines; behind recent lightweight transformers.

== FIGURES ==
[figure fig-compare] 1373x692 — Figure 1 — CTM, a window-wise adaptation, and DQ-CTM compared.
[figure fig-arch] 1373x381 — Figure 2 — ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.
[figure fig-progress] 1298x578 — Figure 4 — Reconstruction at T=0 through T=4 against bicubic and ground truth.
[figure fig-error] 1298x915 — Figure 5 — Absolute-error maps on the same crops, one shared colour scale.

== EQUATIONS ==
[equation eq-carrier] display — \mathbf{F}=\mathcal{E}(\mathbf{I}_{\mathrm{LR}}),\qquad \mathbf{X}=\mathcal{W}(\mathbf{F})

