 DQ-CTM ticks, and decoder as one reconstruction path.","inside":null,"claim":"ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.","evidence":[{"kind":"figure","id":"fig-arch"},{"kind":"section","id":"sec2"}],"narration":"The architecture makes the carrier visible as the object that survives through the method. Encoding starts the path from the low-resolution image. Windowing gives the compact thought process local material to operate on. Shared ticks reuse the same DQ-CTM process across updates. Decoding produces the final reconstruction.","weight":0.86,"seconds":10,"archetype":"annotated-figure","params":{"eyebrow":"End to end","headline":"The carrier persists through the reconstruction path","figureId":"fig-arch","crop":null,"notes":[{"x":0.14,"y":0.48,"text":"Encoder","tone":"a"},{"x":0.38,"y":0.48,"text":"Windows","tone":"b"},{"x":0.62,"y":0.48,"text":"Shared DQ-CTM ticks","tone":"c"},{"x":0.86,"y":0.48,"text":"Decoder","tone":"d"}]}},{"id":"b06-progress","intent":"Reconstruction changes over ticks from T=0 through T=4 and is compared with bicubic and ground truth.","inside":null,"claim":"Reconstruction at T=0 through T=4 against bicubic and ground truth.","evidence":[{"kind":"figure","id":"fig-progress"}],"narration":"The reconstruction figure shows the iterative output rather than a single final image. The zero-tick state anchors the starting reconstruction. Later ticks show how the output changes through time. Bicubic gives the simple interpolation reference. Ground truth gives the target the reconstruction is judged against.","weight":0.72,"seconds":10,"archetype":"annotated-figure","params":{"eyebrow":"Progress over ticks","headline":"The reconstruction is shown across T=0 to T=4","figureId":"fig-progress","crop":null,"notes":[{"x":0.18,"y":0.5,"text":"T=0 start","tone":"a"},{"x":0.43,"y":0.5,"text":"T=1 to T=4 updates","tone":"b"},{"x":0.72,"y":0.5,"text":"Bicubic reference","tone":"c"},{"x":0.9,"y":0.5,"text":"Ground truth target","tone":"d"}]}},{"id":"b07-error","intent":"Absolute-error maps compare the same crops using one shared colour scale.","inside":null,"claim":"Absolute-error maps on the same crops, one shared colour scale.","evidence":[{"kind":"figure","id":"fig-error"}],"narration":"The error maps move the comparison from appearance to pixel-level error. Using the same crops keeps the locations comparable. A shared colour scale makes error magnitude comparable across methods. The figure is therefore about relative error patterns on identical examples.","weight":0.68,"seconds":9,"archetype":"annotated-figure","params":{"eyebrow":"Error maps","headline":"The same crops share one error scale","figureId":"fig-error","crop":null,"notes":[{"x":0.22,"y":0.28,"text":"Same crop set","tone":"a"},{"x":0.62,"y":0.28,"text":"Absolute error","tone":"b"},{"x":0.84,"y":0.78,"text":"Shared colour scale","tone":"c"}]}},{"id":"b08-results","intent":"DQ-CTM-SR is competitive with CNN baselines but trails recent lightweight transformers.","inside":null,"claim":"Competitive with CNN baselines; behind recent lightweight transformers.","evidence":[{"kind":"section","id":"sec3"},{"kind":"table","id":"tbl-bench"}],"narration":"The benchmark places DQ-CTM-SR among lightweight super-resolution methods. CNN baselines sit near the same average score range. CATANet is the recent lightweight transformer reference and scores higher. DQ-CTM-SR uses more parameters than CATANet in this table.","weight":0.9,"seconds":10,"archetype":"data-table","params":{"eyebrow":"Benchmark","headline":"DQ-CTM-SR is competitive but not best","tableId":"tbl-bench","highlight":[{"row":"IMDN","tone":"a"},{"row":"RFDN","tone":"a"},{"row":"CATANet","tone":"c"},{"row":"DQ-CTM-SR","tone":"b"}],"note":"Table 1 reports x4 average over five benchmarks."}},{"id":"b09-params","intent":"DQ-CTM-SR is smaller than CARN but larger than the other listed lightweight baselines.","inside":null,"claim":"DQ-CTM-SR | 1.129M | 28.983","evidence":[{"kind":"table","id":"tbl-bench"}],"narration":"Parameter count gives the cost side of the comparison. CARN is the largest method listed. DQ-CTM-SR is smaller than CARN. IMDN, RFDN, and CATANet all use fewer parameters than DQ-CTM-SR. The table does not present DQ-CTM-SR as the smallest model.","weight":0.6,"seconds":10,"archetype":"bar-compare","params":{"eyebrow":"Model size","headline":"DQ-CTM-SR is not the smallest listed model","unit":"M params","bars":[{"label":"CARN","value":1.592,"tone":"c"},{"label":"DQ-CTM-SR","value":1.129,"tone":"b"},{"label":"IMDN","value":0.715,"tone":"a"},{"label":"RFDN","value":0.55,"tone":"a"},{"label":"CATANet","value":0.535,"tone":"a"}],"note":"Parameter counts come from Table 1."}},{"id":"b10-scores","intent":"DQ-CTM-SR narrowly exceeds CARN and IMDN on average, trails RFDN slightly, and trails CATANet clearly.","inside":null,"claim":"×4 lightweight super-resolution, average over five benchmarks.","evidence":[{"kind":"table","id":"tbl-bench"},{"kind":"section","id":"sec3"}],"narration":"Average score gives the quality side of the comparison. CATANet has the highest reported average. RFDN is slightly ahead of DQ-CTM-SR. DQ-CTM-SR is just above CARN and IMDN. The result supports competitiveness, but not leadership.","weight":0.74,"seconds":10,"archetype":"bar-compare","params":{"eyebrow":"Average score","headline":"CATANet leads the reported average","unit":"average score","bars":[{"label":"CATANet","value":29.482,"tone":"c"},{"label":"RFDN","value":29.022,"tone":"a"},{"label":"DQ-CTM-SR","value":28.983,"tone":"b"},{"label":"CARN","value":28.97,"tone":"a"},{"label":"IMDN","value":28.968,"tone":"a"}],"note":"Average is over five benchmarks."}},{"id":"b11-close","intent":"ThinkSR’s contribution is the dense carrier that lets compact thought operate in a super-resolution pipeline.","inside":null,"claim":"A persistent dense carrier, read and updated by a compact thought process.","evidence":[{"kind":"section","id":"sec2"},{"kind":"section","id":"sec3"}],"narration":"The main idea is architectural: keep the dense field persistent while compact thought updates it. The reported result is competitive with CNN baselines. The same result remains behind recent lightweight transformers.","weight":0.84,"seconds":8,"archetype":"callout","params":{"eyebrow":"Takeaway","headline":"The dense carrier is the core contribution","panels":[{"label":"Mechanism","lines":["Persistent dense carrier","Compact thought updates"]},{"label":"Result","lines":["Competitive with CNN baselines","Behind lightweight transformers"]}],"note":null}}]}
